# UAPK v2.1.1 — CODING AGENT RULES

## Start

For each task read only:

1. `.ai/TASK.md`
2. `.ai/STATE.md`
3. files explicitly listed in TASK

Do not automatically read:

- `BOOT.md`
- all of `.ai/DECISIONS.md`
- unrelated repository files
- old chats/history

If TASK references a decision ID such as D-017:
locate and read only that decision block, stopping at its END marker.

Before editing, check whether the working tree is already dirty.
If unrelated pre-existing changes exist, STOP and report before mixing new work into them.

## Ownership

Coding agent MAY modify:

- source files required by TASK;
- tests required by TASK;
- `.ai/STATE.md`.

Coding agent MUST NOT modify:

- `BOOT.md`
- `.ai/TASK.md`
- `.ai/DECISIONS.md`
- `.clinerules`

This prohibition applies to every editor, tool, script, shell command, redirect, or generated file operation.

If completing TASK appears to require changing a protected file:
STOP and report the conflict.

## Scope

One TASK = one atomic goal.

Do not:

- perform unrelated refactors;
- add unrequested features;
- expand into another subsystem;
- fix unrelated bugs discovered during the task;
- read large unrelated files.

A separate bug/improvement should be recorded briefly in STATE `Next`, not fixed in the current task unless it blocks acceptance.

## Editing

Prefer targeted edits.

If an edit fails:

1. inspect the current relevant code;
2. make one corrected attempt.

Do not repeatedly retry the same failed edit.

## Anti-Loop

A failed attempt belongs to the same unresolved problem when:

- the same acceptance criterion/test still fails; and
- no new root cause has been identified.

Material progress exists only when at least one occurs:

- failure/error meaningfully changes;
- root cause is localized more precisely;
- a previously failing targeted test passes;
- a falsifiable hypothesis narrows the problem.

Another speculative hypothesis alone is NOT progress.

After 2 failed attempts without material progress:

1. STOP.
2. Update STATE with attempts, blocker, and exact next diagnostic step.
3. Do not make a third speculative fix.

## Testing

Order:

1. narrow targeted test;
2. related targeted tests only when necessary;
3. full suite at most once at the end if TASK requires it.

Do not use the full suite as a debugging loop.

## STATE

At successful completion, blocker, or handoff:

- overwrite `.ai/STATE.md`;
- increment VERSION;
- use STATUS only from:
  `NOT_STARTED`, `RUNNING`, `BLOCKED`, `DONE`;
- keep STATE concise: approximately <= 2 KB and <= 50 lines;
- record verified facts and actual test results;
- keep BASELINE_COMMIT fixed to Git HEAD from task start.

Do not append history.
Do not store final commit hash in the same STATE update that will be part of that commit.
Do not cache working-tree clean/dirty state in STATE.

## Truth

- Git HEAD identifies the committed baseline.
- Working tree identifies current uncommitted changes.
- Tests describe only the exact code snapshot on which they ran.
- STATE is a handoff summary and never overrides repository/test evidence.
- Chat is non-canonical.

## Safety

Without explicit TASK authorization:

- no destructive Git operations;
- no deletion of user/production data;
- no production secret changes;
- no force push;
- no paid/external service execution.

Never expose secrets.

## Finish

When acceptance criteria are satisfied:

1. update STATE;
2. report changed files and actual test results;
3. suggest commit `[TASK-ID] description`;
4. STOP.

Do not continue improving the project after TASK is complete.
